    <div class="demo-row">
      <div class="demo-col">

### Creating and Closing a Modal

Call `createModal` to create a modal. It returns a function that can be called to close the modal.

```js
import { createModal } from 'inertiax-ui'

// createModal returns a close function
const closeModal = createModal({
  src: '/modal-content.json',
})

// Navigate back, then unmount
closeModal()

// Or unmount without touching history
closeModal(false)
```
      </div>

      <div class="demo-col">

### Modal Action

You can also use the `use:modal` action, which passes options to `createModal` internally.

```svelte
<a href="/modal-content.json" use:modal>
  Open Modal
</a>
```
      </div>

      <div class="demo-col">

### onclose Callback

Modals accept an `onclose` callback. This callback is invoked when the modal is closed.

```js
import { createModal } from 'inertiax-ui'
import { router } from 'inertiax-svelte'

createModal({
  src: '/profile/edit',
  onclose() {
    router.reload()
  },
})
```

You can also pass `onclose` as an option to the `use:modal` action:

```svelte
<a href="/modal-content.json" use:modal={{ onclose: router.reload }}>
  Open Modal
</a>
```
      </div>

      <div class="demo-col">

### The close() Function

Modal pages receive a `close` function via `$props()`. Call `close()` to navigate back in
history and unmount. Call `close(false)` to just unmount without affecting history.

```svelte
<script>
  const { close } = $props()
</script>

<!-- Navigate back, then unmount -->
<button onclick={close}>Close</button>

<!-- Just unmount, don't touch history -->
<button onclick={() => close(false)}>Close</button>
```
      </div>

      <div class="demo-col">

### Parent Communication

All props passed to `createModal` are forwarded to the page component. Pass callbacks to let
the modal communicate back.

```js
// Parent: pass a callback as a prop
createModal({
  src: '/modal-content.json',
  onSave: (data) => {
    console.log("got data from modal:", data)
  },
})

```

```svelte
// Modal page: receive it via $props()
<script>
  const { onSave, close } = $props()
</script>

<button onclick={close}>Cancel</button>
<button onclick={() => onSave(data)}>Save</button>
```
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

